{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: the "dispatch arm exits before the PR-only stages logic" guard can't actually catch that regression**

`run.indexOf('exit 0')` (this line) returns the **first** `exit 0` in the script — the fail-safe branch's exit at `ci.yml:166`, which sits above the greps and therefore above `ci_fast_gate` regardless of the classifier. If the dispatch arm's own early exit (`ci.yml:196`, the `if [ "${{ github.event_name }}" != "pull_request" ]` guard) is ever removed, dispatches would fall into the PR-only stages logic with empty `BASE_REF`/`HEAD_REF`, and this test would still pass.

Pin the dispatch-exit shape itself instead, e.g.:

```dart
expect(
  run,
  contains('if [ "\${{ github.event_name }}" != "pull_request" ]; then'),
  reason: 'the dispatch arm must exit before the stages classifier',
);
expect(run.indexOf('exit 0'), lessThan(run.indexOf('ci_fast_gate')));
```

(matching the existing literal-assert style of this file), so the guard asserts what its name promises.
